    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-2166",
    ":question/problem": "What is $\\displaystyle \\int\\frac{1}{x^{2}} - 3xdx$?"
  },
  {
    ":db/id": 17592186233643,
    ":question/difficulty": {
      ":db/id": 17592186045485,
      ":db/ident": ":question.difficulty/easy"
    },
    ":question/id": "6b6e2582-e861-5aac-850f-2f62d29905a5",
    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-2251",
    ":question/problem": "Find the antiderivative of $3x+6.$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int 3x+6\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int 6\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+6\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\right)+6(x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}+6x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  },
  {
    ":db/id": 17592186233755,
    ":question/difficulty": {
      ":db/id": 17592186045485,
      ":db/ident": ":question.difficulty/easy"
    },
    ":question/id": "0bf78498-fa41-5c5b-8e73-bc357aed8c2f",
    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-29825",
    ":question/problem": "Find the antiderivative of $3{x}^{2}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}.$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3{x}^{2}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 2{x}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int {x}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\left(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\right)-2\\left(\\frac{{x}^{-2}}{-2}\\right)+C \\\\  & ={x}^{3}+{x}^{-2}+C \\\\  & ={x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  },
  {
    ":db/id": 17592186235391,
    ":question/answer-fields": [
