    ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\int \\sqrt{x}(2+x)\\,\\text{d}x.$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt{x}(2+x)\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{1/2}(2+x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2{x}^{1/2}+{x}^{3/2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int {x}^{1/2}\\text{d}x+\\int {x}^{3/2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\left(\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{2{x}^{5/2}}{5}\\right)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}}{5}+\\frac{4\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  },
