    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-49059",
    ":question/problem": "$\\int \\frac{{x}^{5}+7}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{5}+7}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({x}^{3}+\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int 7{x}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+7\\int {x}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}\\right)+7\\left(\\frac{{x}^{-1}}{-1}\\right)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{7}{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  },
