    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-167617",
    ":question/problem": "Given that $A=2$ and $B=4,$\n\n$\\int \\frac{f(x)}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,C.$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "We found that $A=2$ and $B=4$ in steps 2 and 3, respectively. Hence, $f(x)=2{x}^{2}-4.$  \n\nUsing the sum and constant factor rules and our result from step 4, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{f(x)}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{2{x}^{2}-4}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 2\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x+\\frac{4}{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  },
